      "content": "6.1 Overview of Tribes in Madhya Pradesh"
    },
    {
      "id": "g8zmyd3",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "jfksu2a",
      "src": "/books/Guide/Madhya_Pradesh_GS/images/image_jfksu2a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Madhya Pradesh has the highest Scheduled Tribe (ST) population in India in absolute numbers. Tribal communities constitute approximately 21% of the state's total population. The tribal belt is concentrated primarily in eastern, central-southern, and western parts of the state. The state has 46 Scheduled Tribes, of which several are Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs).",
      "id": "q9ric89"
    },
